// Counter Contract - Locking Script
// State: [count] (serialized after OP_RETURN)
//
// The contract checks the preimage, then checks that the spending
// transaction has one output: this same code, the same amount, and a count
// that is one more or one less than the count being spent. The script cannot
// see which method the panel has selected, so either step passes under
// either name. Any other New State is refused.

// Verify preimage authenticity (OP_PUSH_TX)
checkPreimage

// Keep hashOutputs and the raw 8-byte amount on the alt stack
dup extractOutputHash toAltStack
dup size 52 sub split nip 8 split drop toAltStack

// scriptCode: after the 104-byte head and a 3-byte length, before the
// 52-byte tail. The length is 3 bytes because this script is over 252 bytes.
size 52 sub split drop 107 split nip

// Split the code and its OP_RETURN from the state push.
// CODE LENGTH: the number below is the compiled length of this file plus one.
// Any edit to the code changes it. test/counter-chain.test.js reports the
// right value.
613 split

// Old count. A state push is OP_0, OP_1NEGATE, OP_1 to OP_16, or a length
// byte and the number.
size 1 numEqual if
  dup 0x00 equal if drop 0 else
  dup 0x4f equal if drop -1 else
  bin2num 80 sub endIf endIf
else
  1 split nip bin2num
endIf

// hashOutputs for count + 1
2dup 1add
dup 0 numEqual if drop 0x00 else
dup 1 17 within if 80 add else
dup -1 numEqual if drop 0x4f else
size 1 num2bin swap cat endIf endIf endIf
cat
size 2 num2bin 0xfd swap cat swap cat
fromAltStack dup toAltStack swap cat hash256

// hashOutputs for count - 1
rot rot 1sub
dup 0 numEqual if drop 0x00 else
dup 1 17 within if 80 add else
dup -1 numEqual if drop 0x4f else
size 1 num2bin swap cat endIf endIf endIf
cat
size 2 num2bin 0xfd swap cat swap cat
fromAltStack dup toAltStack swap cat hash256

// The real hashOutputs has to be one of the two
fromAltStack drop fromAltStack
dup rot equal
rot rot equal
boolor
